                <code>maxResults</code>, this value can be used to retrieve the next page of
            results. This value is <code>null</code> when there are no more results to
            return.</p>

            registry_id_output?: str  # <p>The registry ID associated with the request.</p>





    # Clouddirectory Service
    schema ClouddirectoryService:
        """
        Service for clouddirectory resources.
        """


        schema Schema:
            """
            Schema resource
            """

            name: str  # <p>The name that is associated with the schema. This is unique to each account and in each
      region.</p>




        schema Index:
            """
            Index resource
            """

            is_unique: bool  # <p>Indicates whether the attribute that is being indexed has unique values or
      not.</p>

            ordered_indexed_attribute_list: [str]  # <p>Specifies the attributes that should be indexed on. Currently only a single attribute
      is supported.</p>

            parent_reference: str?  # <p>A reference to the parent object that contains the index object.</p>

            directory_arn: str  # <p>The ARN of the directory where the index should be created.</p>

            link_name: str?  # <p>The name of the link between the parent object and the index object.</p>




        schema Object_information:
            """
            ObjectInformation resource
            """



            # Outputs

            schema_facets_output?: [str]  # <p>The facets attached to the specified object. Although the response does not include minor version information, the most recently applied minor version of each Facet is in effect. See <a>GetAppliedSchemaVersion</a> for details.</p>

            object_identifier_output?: str  # <p>The <code>ObjectIdentifier</code> of the specified object.</p>




        schema Object:
            """
            Object resource
            """

            directory_arn: str  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that is associated with the <a>Directory</a>
      in which the object will be created. For more information, see <a>arns</a>.</p>

            object_attribute_list: [str]?  # <p>The attribute map whose attribute ARN contains the key and attribute value as the map
      value.</p>

            parent_reference: str?  # <p>If specified, the parent reference to which this object will be attached.</p>

            schema_facets: [str]  # <p>A list of schema facets to be associated with the object. Do not provide minor version components. See <a>SchemaFacet</a> for details.</p>

            link_name: str?  # <p>The name of link that is used to attach this object to a parent.</p>




        schema Link_attributes:
            """
            LinkAttributes resource
            """

            attribute_updates: [str]  # <p>The attributes update structure.</p>

            directory_arn: str  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that is associated with the Directory where the updated typed link resides. For more information, see <a>arns</a> or <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/clouddirectory/latest/developerguide/directory_objects_links.html#directory_objects_links_typedlink">Typed Links</a>.</p>

            typed_link_specifier: str  # <p>Allows a typed link specifier to be accepted as input.</p>



            # Outputs

            attributes_output?: [str]  # <p>The attributes that are associated with the typed link.</p>




        schema Facet:
            """
            Facet resource
            """

            object_type: str?  # <p>Specifies whether a given object created from this facet is of type node, leaf node,
      policy or index.</p>
         <ul>
            <li>
               <p>Node: Can have multiple children but one parent.</p>
            </li>
         </ul>
         <ul>
            <li>
               <p>Leaf node: Cannot have children but can have multiple parents.</p>
            </li>
         </ul>
         <ul>
            <li>
               <p>Policy: Allows you to store a policy document and policy type. For more
        information, see <a href="https://docs.aws.amazon.com/clouddirectory/latest/developerguide/key_concepts_directory.html#key_concepts_policies">Policies</a>.</p>
            </li>
         </ul>
         <ul>
            <li>
               <p>Index: Can be created with the Index API.</p>
            </li>
         </ul>

            attributes: [str]?  # <p>The attributes that are associated with the <a>Facet</a>.</p>

            schema_arn: str  # <p>The schema ARN in which the new <a>Facet</a> will be created. For more
      information, see <a>arns</a>.</p>

            name: str  # <p>The name of the <a>Facet</a>, which is unique for a given schema.</p>

            facet_style: str?  # <p>There are two different styles that you can define on any given facet, <code>Static</code> and <code>Dynamic</code>. For static facets, all attributes must be defined in the schema. For dynamic facets, attributes can be defined during data plane operations.</p>



            # Outputs

            facet_output?: str  # <p>The <a>Facet</a> structure that is associated with the facet.</p>




        schema Applied_schema_version:
            """
            AppliedSchemaVersion resource
            """



            # Outputs

            applied_schema_arn_output?: str  # <p>Current applied schema ARN, including the minor version in use if one was provided.</p>




        schema Object_attributes:
            """
            ObjectAttributes resource
            """

            object_reference: str  # <p>The reference that identifies the object.</p>

            directory_arn: str  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that is associated with the <a>Directory</a>
      where the object resides. For more information, see <a>arns</a>.</p>

            attribute_updates: [str]  # <p>The attributes update structure.</p>



            # Outputs

            attributes_output?: [str]  # <p>The attributes that are associated with the object.</p>




        schema Schema_from_json:
            """
            SchemaFromJson resource
            """

            schema_arn: str  # <p>The ARN of the schema to update.</p>

            document: str  # <p>The replacement JSON schema.</p>




        schema Schema_as_json:
