      its Amazon Resource Name (ARN). You can also specify a related item associated with a
      resource. For example, to specify an Amazon DynamoDB (DynamoDB) table as a
      resource, use the table's ARN. You can also specify an Amazon CloudWatch metric associated
      with the DynamoDB table as a related item.</p>

            incident_record_arn: str  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the incident record that the action adds the incident
      to.</p>



            # Outputs

            event_output?: str  # <p>Details about the timeline event.</p>




        schema Response_plan:
            """
            ResponsePlan resource
            """

            chat_channel: str?  # <p>The Chatbot chat channel used for collaboration during an incident.</p>

            tags: {str: str}?  # <p>A list of tags that you are adding to the response plan.</p>

            engagements: [str]?  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the contacts and escalation plans that the response
      plan engages during an incident.</p>

            client_token: str?  # <p>A token ensuring that the operation is called only once with the specified details.</p>

            actions: [str]?  # <p>The actions that the response plan starts at the beginning of an incident.</p>

            name: str  # <p>The short format name of the response plan. Can't include spaces.</p>

            integrations: [str]?  # <p>Information about third-party services integrated into the response plan.</p>

            display_name: str?  # <p>The long format of the response plan name. This field can contain spaces.</p>

            incident_template: str  # <p>Details used to create an incident when using this response plan.</p>



            # Outputs

            chat_channel_output?: str  # <p>The Chatbot chat channel used for collaboration during an incident.</p>

            name_output?: str  # <p>The short format name of the response plan. The name can't contain spaces.</p>

            incident_template_output?: str  # <p>Details used to create the incident when using this response plan.</p>

            display_name_output?: str  # <p>The long format name of the response plan. Can contain spaces.</p>

            arn_output?: str  # <p>The ARN of the response plan.</p>

            actions_output?: [str]  # <p>The actions that this response plan takes at the beginning of the incident.</p>

            engagements_output?: [str]  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for the contacts and escalation plans that the response
      plan engages during an incident.</p>

            integrations_output?: [str]  # <p>Information about third-party services integrated into the Incident Manager response
      plan.</p>




        schema Replication_set:
            """
            ReplicationSet resource
            """

            tags: {str: str}?  # <p>A list of tags to add to the replication set.</p>

            client_token: str?  # <p>A token that ensures that the operation is called only once with the specified
      details.</p>

            regions: {str: str}  # <p>The Regions that Incident Manager replicates your data to. You can have up to three Regions in
      your replication set.</p>



