         restore a recovery point.</p>

            expected_completion_time_minutes_output?: int  # <p>The amount of time in minutes that a job restoring a recovery point is expected to
         take.</p>

            validation_status_message_output?: str  # <p>The status message.</p>

            completion_date_output?: str  # <p>The date and time that a job to restore a recovery point is completed, in Unix format
         and Coordinated Universal Time (UTC). The value of <code>CompletionDate</code> is accurate
         to milliseconds. For example, the value 1516925490.087 represents Friday, January 26, 2018
         12:11:30.087 AM.</p>

            backup_size_in_bytes_output?: int  # <p>The size, in bytes, of the restored resource.</p>

            recovery_point_arn_output?: str  # <p>An ARN that uniquely identifies a recovery point; for example,
            <code>arn:aws:backup:us-east-1:123456789012:recovery-point:1EB3B5E7-9EB0-435A-A80B-108B488B0D45</code>.</p>

            backup_vault_arn_output?: str  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the backup vault containing the recovery point being restored. This helps identify vault access policies and permissions.</p>

            source_resource_arn_output?: str  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the original resource that was backed up. This provides context about what resource is being restored.</p>

            status_message_output?: str  # <p>A message showing the status of a job to restore a recovery point.</p>

            resource_type_output?: str  # <p>Returns metadata associated with a restore job listed by resource type.</p>

            percent_done_output?: str  # <p>Contains an estimated percentage that is complete of a job at the time the job status
         was queried.</p>

            account_id_output?: str  # <p>Returns the account ID that owns the restore job.</p>

            validation_status_output?: str  # <p>The status of validation run on the indicated 
         restore job.</p>

            creation_date_output?: str  # <p>The date and time that a restore job is created, in Unix format and Coordinated
         Universal Time (UTC). The value of <code>CreationDate</code> is accurate to milliseconds.
         For example, the value 1516925490.087 represents Friday, January 26, 2018 12:11:30.087
         AM.</p>

            created_resource_arn_output?: str  # <p>The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the resource that 
      was created by the restore job.</p>
         <p>The format of the ARN depends on the resource type of the backed-up
         resource.</p>

            iam_role_arn_output?: str  # <p>Specifies the IAM role ARN used to create the target recovery point; for example,
            <code>arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/S3Access</code>.</p>

            restore_job_id_output?: str  # <p>Uniquely identifies the job that restores a recovery point.</p>

            created_by_output?: str  # <p>Contains identifying information about the creation of a restore job.</p>

            recovery_point_creation_date_output?: str  # <p>The creation date of the recovery point made by the specifed restore job.</p>

            deletion_status_message_output?: str  # <p>This describes the restore job deletion status.</p>




